  "foaf:name": "SeaCountry Education for Environmental Development",
  "sdo:name": "SeaCountry Education for Environmental Development",
  "sdo:description": "The Torres Strait Islands Sea-Country Education for Environmental Development (TSI SEED) Initiative empowers Islanders through Indigenous-led governance, accredited training, and enterprise development. Anchored in island-based training hubs, the program delivers Marine Habitat Conservation and Restoration (MHCR) courses with specialised credentials. Co-designed with Indigenous knowledge holders, training integrates Traditional Ecological Knowledge, languages, and oral traditions with contemporary science, strengthening ocean literacy and cultural identity. TSI SEED restores coastal and marine ecosystems, while reinvigorating food systems to improve nutrition, health, and mental well-being. Youth are supported into careers through enterprise incubation and job placements, building a resilient Indigenous-led blue economy. Scalable and globally relevant, TSI SEED creates a living classroom of ocean stewardship, offering a blueprint for other island nations facing similar challenges.",
